<section class="faq">
    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

    <h3>What items belong in SaaS Cost of Goods Sold (COGS)?</h3>
    <p>SaaS COGS includes AWS/GCP server hosting, database fees, payment gateway transaction charges, third-party API subscriptions integrated into the software, and customer support personnel salaries.</p>

    <h3>What is the difference between gross margin and net margin?</h3>
    <p>Gross margin measures earnings after subtracting direct production COGS. Net margin subtracts all indirect overhead including marketing ad spend, sales payroll, R&D engineering salaries, taxes, and legal fees.</p>
</section>

